  "worked_solution": "To express the number in Cartesian form, we expand the parentheses and substitute the values of the cosine and sine.\n\nSince $\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=0$ and $\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=1$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =2(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{2})) \\\\  & =2(0+\\text{i}) \\\\  & =2\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
